From 88886b7f142912995163fb3c9a277f5cc44c81a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:37:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/26] plugin_api: let pixel plugins pick files through AERA's
 picker

A Host API 3 plugin draws its own pixels, so it has no way to show the
user a file dialog that fits AERA, and recovery has none of the desktop
services a toolkit's dialog relies on (portals, GTK). Picking a file is
basic to most apps; give pixel plugins AERA's picker.

REQUEST_OPERATION with value 8 (kPickFiles) opens components/file_picker
over the surface, advertised as kFeatureFilePicker in HELLO_ACK. flags is
the mode (one file, several, a folder, a name to save as), title the
folder to start in, text the extensions to show or the name to suggest.
Each chosen path comes back as its own OPERATION_RESULT, flags 1 while
more follow, paced a few per tick so a large selection never fills the
control socket; closing the picker answers value 0 with empty text.

The pick needs no permission or prompt: choosing the file is the user's
consent, as with a desktop file dialog, and the plugin is root already.
The other host operations stay with Host API 2's declarative pages.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
